repository-code: 'https://github.com/PennyJClarke/strandings_from_space'
abstract: "A very high-resolution (VHR) satellite image pre-processing and annotation pipeline for stranded whales and dolphins (adaptable to any feature of interest), and a semi-automated multi-observer annotation comparison workflow for evaluating count congruence, for annotations made in geolocated satellite imagery (latitude, longitude) and unknown reference aerial imagery (row, col). The repository includes (1) a step-by-step VHR satellite image pre-processing and annotation workflow for detecting features of interest (geolocated point, bounding box and image chip outputs), developed using QGIS 3.28, (2) a replicable step-by-step VHR satellite image pre-processing and annotation workflow in Python 3.10, and (3) a data standard for the ‘satellites to study stranded cetaceans’ community, including a template for recording annotation metadata and accompanying training document, to enable data sharing internationally."
